<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Mithridatic War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">73–<a href="/years/63-bce">63 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Mithridatic War of 73–63 BCE was the last war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a>. It began when Mithridates invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bithynia">Bithynia</a>, which its last king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicomedes-iv">Nicomedes IV</a> had bequeathed to Rome. Lucullus drove him from Pontus, Roman forces seized Greek cities on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> completed the war; Mithridates killed himself in 63 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-mithridatic-war.jpg" alt="Third Mithridatic War" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ilya Yakubovich · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1stMithritadicwar89BC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
